COMPILE ERROR: reinterpret_cast from uint8_t* to address_space(3) uint8_t* is not allowed.

The fix: use C-style cast for LDS address space conversion:
```cpp
// WRONG:
as3_uint8_p lds_ptr = reinterpret_cast<as3_uint8_p>(smem);

// CORRECT (from submission_amd_blog_v2.py which COMPILES):
as3_uint8_p lds_ptr = (as3_uint8_p)(smem);
```

OR define the LDS pointer type differently:
```cpp
__shared__ uint8_t smem[SIZE];
// Use smem directly — __shared__ already implies address_space(3)
```

Read submission_amd_blog_v2.py to see how it handles the LDS pointer casts — it COMPILES successfully.

Fix and resubmit as submission_pingpong_small_v2.py.

